    {
      "id": "xr9y6Pxh_MW28IDvoVvE3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2530.9277312640215,
      "y": 7557.853933254822,
      "width": 1243,
      "height": 1975,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#9c36b5",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b00",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 386517017,
      "version": 2177,
      "versionNonce": 280026583,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1769682103251,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "N floor building\nTwo elevators\n\n1, 2, 3, 4, ......N\n\nFunctionality\n\n- Kind of Request: Person is outside a lift and requesting for a lift from a floor\n- Lift reached and he selected a floor he has to go\n\n- Request Direction: Up/ Down\n- Lift Direction: Up/Down/Idle State\n\nCentral System\n- Queue (Requests)\n\n5th floor - Go Down\nThere are two lifts\nOne is going up (Request 10) [G floor] (G -> 10)\nOne is coming down from floor greater than 5 (> 5)\n\n- Optimal way of serving all the requests\n- (User source floor, Direction)\n\n(1, Up) (3, up) (5, down) (6, up) (2, down)\n\n- Priority queue (serving the requests)\n- Lift movement consideration\n\n- Up -> all the requestion for up direction within path will be taken care by this lift\n\n\nElevatorSystemController\n\n- lifts = new Map() # liftId: Lift\n- requests = new Map() # id: Request\n- requestAssignments = [(r1, l1), (r2, l2), (r3, l1)] (queue)\n- lift - Up/Dowm\n\n- request(source, direction):\n    - new Request(s, d)\n    - this.requests.set(id, request)\n    \n\n- processRequest():\n    - every x second (changing params, Lift movement)\n    - for(lift in lifts):\n        if(lift.currentDirection == 'UP'):\n            # assign all the requests which are in 'UP' direction and greater than lift ka current floor (filter)\n            # Sort (in ascending)\n        elif('Down)\n            # assign requests which are in 'Down' direction\n            # Sort\n        else:\n            liftCurrentFloor\n            # either assign all the requests grater than this current floor\n            # all the requests less then the current floor\n- l\n            \n            \n\nLift\n--\nid\ncurrentDirection: UP/DOWN/IDLE\ncurrentFloor\n\n\nRequest\n- id\n- source floor\n- dest direction\n- isServed\n- lift: 1/2\n\n \n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "N floor building\nTwo elevators\n\n1, 2, 3, 4, ......N\n\nFunctionality\n\n- Kind of Request: Person is outside a lift and requesting for a lift from a floor\n- Lift reached and he selected a floor he has to go\n\n- Request Direction: Up/ Down\n- Lift Direction: Up/Down/Idle State\n\nCentral System\n- Queue (Requests)\n\n5th floor - Go Down\nThere are two lifts\nOne is going up (Request 10) [G floor] (G -> 10)\nOne is coming down from floor greater than 5 (> 5)\n\n- Optimal way of serving all the requests\n- (User source floor, Direction)\n\n(1, Up) (3, up) (5, down) (6, up) (2, down)\n\n- Priority queue (serving the requests)\n- Lift movement consideration\n\n- Up -> all the requestion for up direction within path will be taken care by this lift\n\n\nElevatorSystemController\n\n- lifts = new Map() # liftId: Lift\n- requests = new Map() # id: Request\n- requestAssignments = [(r1, l1), (r2, l2), (r3, l1)] (queue)\n- lift - Up/Dowm\n\n- request(source, direction):\n    - new Request(s, d)\n    - this.requests.set(id, request)\n    \n\n- processRequest():\n    - every x second (changing params, Lift movement)\n    - for(lift in lifts):\n        if(lift.currentDirection == 'UP'):\n            # assign all the requests which are in 'UP' direction and greater than lift ka current floor (filter)\n            # Sort (in ascending)\n        elif('Down)\n            # assign requests which are in 'Down' direction\n            # Sort\n        else:\n            liftCurrentFloor\n            # either assign all the requests grater than this current floor\n            # all the requests less then the current floor\n- l\n            \n            \n\nLift\n--\nid\ncurrentDirection: UP/DOWN/IDLE\ncurrentFloor\n\n\nRequest\n- id\n- source floor\n- dest direction\n- isServed\n- lift: 1/2\n\n \n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "u_mXY9zuJ66n-vgClVT_1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2580.0292951506585,
      "y": 9817.449169569529,
      "width": 363,
      "height": 625,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#9c36b5",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b01",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2107481305,
      "version": 248,
      "versionNonce": 2058136825,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1769683207781,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1 person - 1R (2nd Floor, Up)\n\n(1 lift - 6) (2 Lift - 1)\n\n\nLift State\n- Movement of lift (Up/Down/Idle)\n- current floor (Int)\n\n- ------- \n\n- 1 UDI\n2 UDI\n3 UDI\n\n3n\n\n- -\n3n * 3n \n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1 person - 1R (2nd Floor, Up)\n\n(1 lift - 6) (2 Lift - 1)\n\n\nLift State\n- Movement of lift (Up/Down/Idle)\n- current floor (Int)\n\n- ------- \n\n- 1 UDI\n2 UDI\n3 UDI\n\n3n\n\n- -\n3n * 3n \n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
