      "updated": 1775057364460,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Queue",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "-yL0SqO0bdIl8yWYGM9p-",
      "originalText": "Queue",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ABkVOMGLCDpegJ-WJQjf6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2924.615318482614,
      "y": 19255.65080747188,
      "width": 968,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#9c36b5",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1a",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1542966882,
      "version": 608,
      "versionNonce": 1728918626,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1775057628876,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Asynchronous Processing\n2. We dont want our processor to get overloaded,\nit can process at its own pace\n3. Secondly if anything go wrongs in processing, the recordings will remain in the\nqueue to take it and process it again\n4. Kafka ensures that atleast one time delivery\n5. If consumers fails after processing the message, but before commiting its offset\n5. On restart, it can get the message again from Kafka, however we have to take care of \nits idempotency (Some way to make sure we dont process it again)\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Asynchronous Processing\n2. We dont want our processor to get overloaded,\nit can process at its own pace\n3. Secondly if anything go wrongs in processing, the recordings will remain in the\nqueue to take it and process it again\n4. Kafka ensures that atleast one time delivery\n5. If consumers fails after processing the message, but before commiting its offset\n5. On restart, it can get the message again from Kafka, however we have to take care of \nits idempotency (Some way to make sure we dont process it again)\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
