      "text": "RingCentral",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "J9rLIzhlKBOmNPsb3OU7l",
      "originalText": "RingCentral",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ezmrHQjDXZdrRR6YSRyp1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2044.673214716785,
      "y": 21026.565785858318,
      "width": 934.8343158096541,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#9c36b5",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1r",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1269586558,
      "version": 442,
      "versionNonce": 1988967678,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1775107592557,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Admin opens the Zoom MarketPlace\n2. Searches for AI Conversation Expert.\n3. Click Add/Install\n4. Zoom gives the Secret key which needs to be\nused to communicate to Zoom.\n    Zoom sends the secret token in each event notification we send to your app.\n    Note: This secret token is used to verify event notifications sent by Zoom\n5. Provide the RingCentral URL where Zoom will send the data\n6. Subscribe to events (For Zoom to know for which events they need to send the\ndata)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Admin opens the Zoom MarketPlace\n2. Searches for AI Conversation Expert.\n3. Click Add/Install\n4. Zoom gives the Secret key which needs to be\nused to communicate to Zoom.\n    Zoom sends the secret token in each event notification we send to your app.\n    Note: This secret token is used to verify event notifications sent by Zoom\n5. Provide the RingCentral URL where Zoom will send the data\n6. Subscribe to events (For Zoom to know for which events they need to send the data)",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "jbW1gvvizOBeujuRU__fP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3178.7174319413757,
      "y": 20983.30942034617,
      "width": 1243,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#9c36b5",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1t",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1889370046,
      "version": 1216,
      "versionNonce": 363331916,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1775113535902,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Enables the Zoom Integration on RingCentral Admin Portal\n2. Preparing a system to receive and process data\n3. The Admin goes to \"RingSense\" section of the Portal\n4. Locate the Third Party Integrations and find \"Zoom\"\n5. When user clicks on \"Connect Zoom\", RingCentral sends your browser\nto Zoom Authorisation Server with Specific Url.\n6. https://zoom.us/oauth/authorize?response_type=code&client_id=\n[RC_CLIENT_ID]&redirect_uri=[RC_CALLBACK_URL]&scope=recording:read meeting:read user:read\n7. Users login to Zoom, it sees \"RingCentral is requesting access to your recordings\"\n    - Zoom takes client_id and checks its database\n    - It compares the redirect uri character by character against the Url RingCentral provided while registration\n    - It also checks for scope, it should match the same provided by the user during registration \n8. Click Allow to give access\n9. It redirects the browser to your RingCentral Callback url attaching Authorisation code\nat the end\n10. Ring Central backend sends a \"POST\" request to Zoom backend with this Authorisation code\n11. Zoom sends two tokens (Access Token - Short Lived Token for calling API calls)\n12. Refresh Tokens: Long Lived Token (Used to get new Access Token once the old one expires)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Enables the Zoom Integration on RingCentral Admin Portal\n2. Preparing a system to receive and process data\n3. The Admin goes to \"RingSense\" section of the Portal\n4. Locate the Third Party Integrations and find \"Zoom\"\n5. When user clicks on \"Connect Zoom\", RingCentral sends your browser\nto Zoom Authorisation Server with Specific Url.\n6. https://zoom.us/oauth/authorize?response_type=code&client_id=\n[RC_CLIENT_ID]&redirect_uri=[RC_CALLBACK_URL]&scope=recording:read meeting:read user:read\n7. Users login to Zoom, it sees \"RingCentral is requesting access to your recordings\"\n    - Zoom takes client_id and checks its database\n    - It compares the redirect uri character by character against the Url RingCentral provided while registration\n    - It also checks for scope, it should match the same provided by the user during registration \n8. Click Allow to give access\n9. It redirects the browser to your RingCentral Callback url attaching Authorisation code\nat the end\n10. Ring Central backend sends a \"POST\" request to Zoom backend with this Authorisation code\n11. Zoom sends two tokens (Access Token - Short Lived Token for calling API calls)\n12. Refresh Tokens: Long Lived Token (Used to get new Access Token once the old one expires)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xiJlV0uMjqUloj0pHalgJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2105.442860977295,
      "y": 21452.084115239206,
      "width": 1188,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#9c36b5",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2100126306,
      "version": 437,
      "versionNonce": 1504136820,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1775113123101,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Data Retrieval\n1. The moment your zoom recording finishes processing in the cloud, Zoom sends a webhook to RingCentrals URL\n2. {\"event\": \"recording.completed\", \"payload\": {\"object\": {\"uuid\": \"12345\", \"meeting_id\": \"987654321\"}}}\n3. RingCentral uses its stored \"access token\" to call the API GET /meetings/987654321/recordings\n4. Zoom responds with list of files (audio, video and chat) and download url for each\n5. RingCentral attaches the access token/download token to download the file making use of download url",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Data Retrieval\n1. The moment your zoom recording finishes processing in the cloud, Zoom sends a webhook to RingCentrals URL\n2. {\"event\": \"recording.completed\", \"payload\": {\"object\": {\"uuid\": \"12345\", \"meeting_id\": \"987654321\"}}}\n3. RingCentral uses its stored \"access token\" to call the API GET /meetings/987654321/recordings\n4. Zoom responds with list of files (audio, video and chat) and download url for each\n5. RingCentral attaches the access token/download token to download the file making use of download url",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TIxP00Avfe6vqbcSGvrh6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2549.276559593846,
      "y": 19296.94040742177,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#9c36b5",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1x",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2060839244,
      "version": 167,
      "versionNonce": 334168948,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1775121339925,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Given the volume of recordings\nIngestion layer must remain \nstateless. At this volume you\ncant perform business logic\nYou must perform \nVerify -> Enqueue -> Ack",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Given the volume of recordings\nIngestion layer must remain \nstateless. At this volume you\ncant perform business logic\nYou must perform \nVerify -> Enqueue -> Ack",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
