      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Recordings\nIngestor(Zoom)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "eKhxvHDoYvXL-uAHfDQb4",
      "originalText": "Recordings Ingestor(Zoom)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Pu2CLpotGz9EwGnrVQ2K-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2359.2566816063286,
      "y": 22356.375157969112,
      "width": 627,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#9c36b5",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2E",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 929766260,
      "version": 240,
      "versionNonce": 741595084,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1775123014229,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We can scale things independently\nIf any service fails or lots of events are received,\nthen we can scale that service independently, also other \nservice will remain unaffected.\n99.999% uptime (availability)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We can scale things independently\nIf any service fails or lots of events are received,\nthen we can scale that service independently, also other \nservice will remain unaffected.\n99.999% uptime (availability)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "jOhnuB0fTwO_H1Plihug3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2329.954881000443,
      "y": 22502.848816575897,
      "width": 1518,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#9c36b5",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 95738700,
      "version": 1381,
      "versionNonce": 714150092,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1775131554879,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Failure scenario\n- Zoom has a minor outage and then suddenly sends 10millions delayed events.\n- In order to prevent our system to crash, the gateway can return 503 service unavailable, asking it to retry again\nwith \"Retry After\" which tells the system when they should retry again\n- At the scale, we should build reconcilation system, which daily at 2am for example, should get list of all recordings\nand check against it database for 503 failure, if yes, then pull the recording manually.\n- Someone discovers your webhook URL and floods with 10GB of junk data, we should limit the payload size and reject it if \ngreater than say 1MB\n- There is a possibility same events are sent twice on webhooks (In order to make sure we dont ingest it multiple times\nwe will check for the key in our redis, if it is there with status \"ingested\", ignore the request, otherwise create it with TTL \n\nSecurity of webhooks\n- HMAC (Hash based Message Authentication Code) is sent in webhooks\n- Zoom encrypts the payload and uses the client key to create a signature.\n- At RingCentral side, it tries to create same signature using secret key and payload, if it matches, it is good, otherwise it is tampered\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Failure scenario\n- Zoom has a minor outage and then suddenly sends 10millions delayed events.\n- In order to prevent our system to crash, the gateway can return 503 service unavailable, asking it to retry again\nwith \"Retry After\" which tells the system when they should retry again\n- At the scale, we should build reconcilation system, which daily at 2am for example, should get list of all recordings\nand check against it database for 503 failure, if yes, then pull the recording manually.\n- Someone discovers your webhook URL and floods with 10GB of junk data, we should limit the payload size and reject it if \ngreater than say 1MB\n- There is a possibility same events are sent twice on webhooks (In order to make sure we dont ingest it multiple times\nwe will check for the key in our redis, if it is there with status \"ingested\", ignore the request, otherwise create it with TTL \n\nSecurity of webhooks\n- HMAC (Hash based Message Authentication Code) is sent in webhooks\n- Zoom encrypts the payload and uses the client key to create a signature.\n- At RingCentral side, it tries to create same signature using secret key and payload, if it matches, it is good, otherwise it is tampered\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
